  "observations": {
    "close": "Clear visible gain: individually readable fine pebbles and friable dry soil replace the smoother faintly directional sand surface. Relief remains restrained; the previous dark pit-chain look is absent. This is a texture and material improvement, not merely a tint change.",
    "middle": "Bare lots gain fine texture and modest irregular tonal breaks while retaining a dry pale ground appearance. They still share a broad similar surface, with limited readable separation of compacted, loose and pad roles.",
    "wide": "The palette remains coherent with the existing scene. Ground at this distance is still broadly pale and low in detail; faint directional texture repetition and broad angular patches remain visible, especially outside the building clusters. The bounded change does not resolve those features.",
    "unchanged_scene": "Building silhouettes, road/sidewalk geometry and sharp edge transitions appear consistent with the matched before views. Their separate defects are not counted as ground-material improvement."
  },
